WEBVTT

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:04.820
<i>As long as I'm alive,</i>

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:09.660
<i>I don't give a shit about some dead guy's feelings,</i>

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:11.200
<i>and I don't wanna understand 'em, either.</i>

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:28.170
Salty...

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:35.640
Where am I?

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:37.930
What the...

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:41.350
I'm cast away?

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:51.780
What the hell is this?

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.410
It's even more like a fairy tale than Hanayashiki.

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:11.260
I didn't care what our future together would have been like

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:17.430
as we'd have sat close enough to know the other's feelings

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:23.980
I was prepared for the time you left

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:30.820
but still I found no words to encourage you

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:37.330
After I embraced you with all I had

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:46.880
a sadness that may well have been our closeness

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:50.550
filled my heart

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:57.050
Saying goodbye was for the best

00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:03.730
You gave me happiness

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:07.060
Until I meet you again one day

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:09.570
Until I know what you are truly like

00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:12.110
Summer Snow Rendezvous
Until I know what you are truly like

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:16.840
I won't forget your smile
Summer Snow Rendezvous

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:17.910
I won't forget your smile

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:05.660
Manager?!

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.790
The manager when she was younger!

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:10.670
Why?

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:20.800
Up... we go.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:22.180
Ciao!

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:24.600
What is this?

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:29.190
Manager...

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:31.070
Yes?

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:32.940
You really cut back on our stock, huh?

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:35.780
The flowers.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:38.110
Yeah.

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:43.330
Now that the civic center's moved from the end of the street to Kitamachi,

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:46.330
we're not getting as many orders for bouquets.

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:48.960
Shame. I know you like arranging bouquets.

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:50.580
Well, what can I do?

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:53.250
Make one and I'll buy it.

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:56.470
The base should be... I know.

00:03:57.050 --> 00:03:58.470
Big flowers would be good.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:00.260
What would you recommend today?

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:03.760
Maybe several new varieties of tulips?

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:04.930
They're cute.

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:05.970
Okay, use those.

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:08.440
About how many?

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:10.230
Say about 5,000 yen worth.

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:12.360
Certainly.

00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:17.240
Who lends people their husband's shirt?

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:19.820
Sorry. I know it's old.

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:23.240
Can I keep this shirt?

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:28.750
Your clothes are in the dryer now, on high.

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:29.960
They'll be dry soon.

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:31.290
Okay.

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:33.460
Sorry.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:35.500
It's all right.

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:41.970
<i>I told you...</i>

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:46.220
<i>to throw away all my stuff.</i>

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:48.390
<i>You're so silly,</i>

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:50.230
<i>Rokka.</i>

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:52.230
What about the ribbons?

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:54.230
You decide.

00:04:54.570 --> 00:04:56.610
You're kind of a lazy customer.

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:00.030
I want you to choose.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.610
And you've got a silver tongue.

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:05.280
<i>To think, we're still just as far apart,</i>

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:08.910
<i>but when I say something to her, she actually answers me.</i>

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:12.670
Okay, finished.

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:26.890
You have them.

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:32.850
<i>To be able to give her a bouquet again like this...</i>

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:36.320
<i>Maybe it's a dream.</i>

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:40.860
<i>Crap. She's too cute.</i>

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:46.120
Traveler, did you happen to see the prince?

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:48.540
It finally hit me.

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:51.410
Manager, are you cosplaying as Thumbelina?

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:52.710
Thumbelina?

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:55.250
She was born from a tulip.

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:57.880
What kind of flower were you born from?

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:01.220
What the heck? You're talking like a fairy?

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:03.970
Would you help me search for him?

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:06.430
The thing of it is, Princess,

00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:09.890
I still haven't wrapped my head around this world.

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:11.230
Please.

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:13.310
Sure.

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:22.440
I must have said something to the ghost without thinking.

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:29.120
<i>W-Why is he crying?</i>

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:31.370
Ow!

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:32.290
Huh?

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:37.790
You've got bunny eyes!

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:38.750
Why?

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:40.300
That's what I want to ask you.

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:42.550
Ow... Ouch!

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:45.130
Did dust get in there?

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:47.050
I don't think you should rub them.

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:50.640
It's like... Ow!

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:53.430
Would you take a look?

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:03.240
Maybe it's your contacts?

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:07.200
<i>Hazuki has bad eyes?</i>

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:08.950
Why don't you take them out?

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:11.330
<i>I don't know how.</i>

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:13.790
I wonder if that's the cause.

00:07:13.790 --> 00:07:15.080
I don't know, but...

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:18.790
<i>Why is this throwing cold water on the moving reunion between me and my wife?</i>

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:20.670
<i>Hazuki's stupid eyes!</i>

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:22.460
You'll scratch your eyeballs...

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:24.210
I'm scared!

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:26.720
I already have a fear of pointy things!

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:28.220
Stop acting like a child.

00:07:29.090 --> 00:07:30.850
Just go use the bathroom.

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:41.230
<i>He's totally drunk.</i>

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:43.610
<i>I mean, he's acting weird.</i>

00:07:45.610 --> 00:07:46.900
Got them out...

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:48.860
Yeah. Now I'm good.

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:52.490
<i>Now that I look at him again like this,</i>

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:55.370
<i>He sure is young.</i>

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:58.960
<i>His skin is ridiculously smooth.</i>

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:01.670
<i>He must be quite healthy.</i>

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:03.670
<i>I'll give him a flick.</i>

00:08:05.090 --> 00:08:06.590
Over here...

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:09.760
Ow!

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:16.770
What's happening?!

00:08:16.770 --> 00:08:17.730
Is something wrong?

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:19.980
Everything a few feet away is blurry.

00:08:19.980 --> 00:08:21.770
The world is hazy.

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:23.400
Did you take out the contacts?

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:24.110
Yeah.

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:26.530
But I didn't think my vision was this bad.

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:30.030
Where are they?

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:31.660
Here.

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:33.530
They're torn up.

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:35.410
Really? Both of them?

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:38.160
Yeah. And all squished.

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:39.960
Maybe I won't be able to use them again.

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:41.790
That's probably a safe bet.

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:45.050
Um...

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:46.300
Yes?

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:49.220
Can I spend the night here?

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:50.550
What are you saying?!

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:54.640
<i>After all, not only do I not know where Hazuki lives,</i>

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:56.930
<i>but my vision is so fuzzy that I don't wanna take one step.</i>

00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:59.980
I'll sleep in the shop, so please...

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:01.850
I can't have that...

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:05.940
Yeah, I can understand that...

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:07.730
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:10.610
<i>What do I do about the contact lenses?</i>

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:13.450
<i>How do you get a pair of glasses made?</i>

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:17.830
How much did you drink?

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:19.580
Why don't you lie down for a little while?

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:20.830
Don't say that!

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:22.960
<i>You're</i> the one who wanted to stay over...

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:26.750
You don't know what this guy will do when he's drunk!

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:28.460
Then what should we do?!

00:09:29.550 --> 00:09:31.630
Be happy.

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:33.760
What's that mean?

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:37.010
"What should we do?"

00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:40.520
<i>If I knew the answer to that, I wouldn't be a ghost.</i>

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:42.690
Rokka.

00:09:42.690 --> 00:09:45.270
Again, why are you calling me that?

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:46.270
Answer me!

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:49.320
Rokka.

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:50.030
Yes?

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:52.610
Rokka.

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:53.360
Yes.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:55.240
Rokka.

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:56.370
That's me.

00:09:58.120 --> 00:09:59.620
Rokka!

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:01.040
What?

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:03.290
Thank you.

00:10:06.130 --> 00:10:07.290
I'm sorry.

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:10.420
I'm sorry.

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:12.380
Rokka.

00:10:17.890 --> 00:10:19.430
Hazuki.

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:23.270
Stop calling me that.

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:25.650
It just...

00:10:26.610 --> 00:10:27.860
feels a little weird.

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:32.400
My apologies... Manager.

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:42.750
Good morning!

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:51.130
<i>Sis...</i>

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:52.840
Hazuki?

00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:55.680
Good morning.

00:10:56.430 --> 00:10:59.140
Morning... Did you sleep here?

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:01.140
Were you working?

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:05.140
<i>Glasses!</i>

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:07.400
How do you get them made?!

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:08.360
What?

00:11:08.360 --> 00:11:09.520
Those glasses!

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:10.730
At the optician's shop.

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:13.900
That's not what you meant?

00:11:14.990 --> 00:11:19.320
<i>Shit. I wanna get the geekiest-looking pair I can find,</i>

00:11:19.870 --> 00:11:22.990
<i>but all the ones I can afford have decent designs.</i>

00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:27.500
<i>Hazuki's wallet is empty now...</i>

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:29.670
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:11:32.130 --> 00:11:33.170
<i>This is...</i>

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:42.390
What the hell is this?

00:11:43.310 --> 00:11:45.390
Does he intend to open a plant shop?

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:48.980
I wonder if he bought them at the shop...

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:58.200
No bath in here?

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:04.410
Hey, Princess...

00:12:05.290 --> 00:12:07.160
You're so cute riding my shoulder.

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:09.290
It's putting me through the wringer.

00:12:12.380 --> 00:12:15.050
I wish we could convince people that bringing house plants

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:17.420
on a hospital visit is not bad luck.

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:20.140
Spoken like a true florist.

00:12:20.140 --> 00:12:22.550
The idea that the patient will be "rooted" to the hospital room is pure superstition.

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:28.020
This room gets so much sunshine that it's a waste not to fill it with plants.

00:12:28.020 --> 00:12:28.890
Yeah, well...

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:33.860
A long time ago, when I was hospitalized just like this,

00:12:33.860 --> 00:12:36.610
for homework I was keeping an observational diary on a sponge gourd,

00:12:37.530 --> 00:12:39.900
but my dad made me stop because it would supposedly "root me" to the room.

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:46.040
I felt bad, since my friend visited me and brought the seeds.

00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:48.290
When I finally planted them in the ground two years later,

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:54.420
I was envious of everyone else, bringing home heavy-looking, green, square flowerpots.

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:59.010
Everyone walked by me on the way to field day and the school trip,

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:03.550
while I became an expert at giving up.

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:15.400
<i>It's dangerous to bury things you can't change and dejected feelings in the darkness.</i>

00:13:16.860 --> 00:13:19.070
<i>The tough seeds you thought you buried</i>

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:22.160
<i>will sprout after you've forgotten about them.</i>

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:28.290
In picture books and kids' drawings, tulips are drawn modestly,

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:35.000
but in real life, they're huge and have plenty of punch when in bloom, you know?

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:36.630
I think it depends on the type.

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:39.840
I'm back.

00:13:41.930 --> 00:13:42.720
Who are you?

00:13:44.930 --> 00:13:46.510
What the heck?

00:13:46.510 --> 00:13:49.020
I'm Hazuki, your young part-timer.

00:13:49.020 --> 00:13:50.930
You really changed your image.

00:13:51.310 --> 00:13:55.650
I'm positive my vision got weak from having my bangs hanging over my eyes.

00:13:55.650 --> 00:13:57.440
Huh...

00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:01.820
Dorky, right? Tell me I look dorky!

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:04.110
You look dorky.

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:06.950
Did you cut your hair yourself?

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:08.370
That's right.

00:14:08.370 --> 00:14:09.990
I have no money and no hair.

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:12.410
I'm a man who's only got his youth going for him.

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:14.120
Wow.

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:15.080
You did a good job.

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:19.840
Certainly, it must've been annoying to have your hair in your eyes.

00:14:20.090 --> 00:14:21.510
<i>Is this backfiring?!</i>

00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:23.840
<i>Come to think of it, my hair was in my eyes, too!</i>

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:26.180
This was unexpected.

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:27.390
Yeah, I know.

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:31.020
<i>Seeing Hazuki's room</i>

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:36.650
<i>made me feel like I was looking at a profile of a brave, bashful, poor young man.</i>

00:14:37.770 --> 00:14:40.440
What a hackneyed miracle. Jesus...

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:43.650
<i>Even if I was wrong taking it out on him,</i>

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:45.860
<i>this hair will regrow.</i>

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:48.530
I don't need sympathy from a ghost.

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:50.450
<i>I'll let it</i>

00:14:51.580 --> 00:14:53.120
<i>keep growing and growing.</i>

00:14:57.830 --> 00:15:00.300
We walked here before.

00:15:00.300 --> 00:15:01.250
That's a mystery.

00:15:01.840 --> 00:15:04.670
I wonder when your ghost husband will be satisfied.

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:05.930
I don't know.

00:15:05.930 --> 00:15:07.470
That's a mystery.

00:15:07.470 --> 00:15:11.260
We've been walking all this time, but for some reason I'm not tired.

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:14.520
The world is a big ball of mysteries, isn't it?

00:15:14.520 --> 00:15:17.810
Although the biggest mystery is right here.

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:19.520
We haven't found the prince yet, huh?

00:15:20.110 --> 00:15:21.980
Maybe this isn't the right page.

00:15:23.820 --> 00:15:25.990
Page? What do you mean?

00:15:25.990 --> 00:15:28.280
Maybe he's on another page.

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:29.700
What page?

00:15:39.790 --> 00:15:42.550
<i>Normal size and more cosplaying.</i>

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:46.300
The little prince who had too much time on his hands

00:15:46.840 --> 00:15:49.510
carried a colored pencil instead of a sword.

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:50.300
Huh?

00:15:50.890 --> 00:15:53.220
He used a sketchbook as a shield.

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:54.970
What are you talking about?

00:15:55.730 --> 00:15:59.980
He said there was a really long shaded path on the side of the hospital,

00:16:00.440 --> 00:16:03.690
and every single day, he could see his classmates

00:16:03.690 --> 00:16:06.070
through the spaces between the leaves, walking by.

00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:10.910
Unable to even call out to them, he just gazed on as they went by.

00:16:12.080 --> 00:16:15.870
But he didn't want his family to know about that,

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:21.250
so he began keeping this tree shade observational diary as a last-ditch measure.

00:16:22.380 --> 00:16:26.710
Through all four seasons, that tree-lined path changed appearances dramatically,

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:29.970
which delighted the prince's eyes and comforted him.

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:33.680
His sketchbooks were piling up.

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:38.770
Apparently at one point, he couldn't stand having that many around

00:16:39.480 --> 00:16:41.770
and turned them in to be recycled.

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:43.610
All of them?

00:16:43.610 --> 00:16:44.480
That's right.

00:16:45.360 --> 00:16:47.070
He realized it too late.

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:51.570
There were always cool words on his lips,

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:54.830
but really, he was gripping the sponge gourd seeds.

00:16:54.830 --> 00:16:55.620
<i>Sponge gourd?</i>

00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:58.660
I think he was re-evaluating his life and living to the utmost.

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:03.080
He pretended that everything was fine, to the point where you can tell he hated losing.

00:17:04.630 --> 00:17:07.300
But that's what I loved about him.

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:13.010
Manager?

00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:16.560
I don't think I'm the Manager that you know.

00:17:18.220 --> 00:17:19.810
Have you come to abduct me?

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:23.690
Do you intend to abandon me?

00:17:23.690 --> 00:17:25.060
W-Wait a second!

00:17:25.060 --> 00:17:26.730
Are you going to propose to me?

00:17:27.860 --> 00:17:30.860
Look, a swallow is injured!

00:17:37.870 --> 00:17:41.160
So, where are we?

00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:44.920
An unfinished scene.

00:17:45.840 --> 00:17:47.800
Could you be just a little more specific?

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:50.300
An unfinished picture book.

00:17:52.010 --> 00:17:55.140
When the prince became an adult, he still hadn't learned his lesson,

00:17:55.140 --> 00:17:58.140
and again confined various things to paper.

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:04.020
We're back!

00:18:04.020 --> 00:18:05.610
I think it's gonna rain.

00:18:05.980 --> 00:18:07.480
You're back!

00:18:08.320 --> 00:18:09.530
Did you have lunch?

00:18:09.530 --> 00:18:11.360
Yeah. The fried rice combo.

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:12.820
How about you, Hazuki?

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:15.200
I ate too, at a place over there...

00:18:18.490 --> 00:18:21.450
I hope it doesn't rain too hard...

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:24.040
Good night.

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:24.830
See you next week!

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:25.380
Yep.

00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:30.050
Is something wrong?

00:18:31.050 --> 00:18:34.300
Could I have an advance on my wages?

00:18:36.890 --> 00:18:38.180
I'm so ashamed.

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:40.520
You didn't eat lunch either, did you?

00:18:40.520 --> 00:18:41.810
I'm so ashamed.

00:18:41.810 --> 00:18:42.930
Yeah, yeah.

00:18:43.770 --> 00:18:47.940
<i>Why do I have to feed Hazuki Rokka's homemade cooking?!</i>

00:18:48.770 --> 00:18:51.320
<i>Shit! I hate Hazuki's empty stomach!</i>

00:18:52.280 --> 00:18:53.570
Here you go.

00:18:54.030 --> 00:18:54.950
Thank you.

00:18:54.950 --> 00:18:56.490
Let's eat!

00:18:58.830 --> 00:19:00.450
When was the last time you ate?

00:19:01.540 --> 00:19:03.500
Nothing. Never mind.

00:19:29.770 --> 00:19:32.940
<i>I know this table.</i>

00:19:34.240 --> 00:19:36.070
<i>The feeling of someone in front of me,</i>

00:19:37.280 --> 00:19:41.620
<i>glimpses of Shimao's utensils moving out of the corner of my eye...</i>

00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:46.500
I love this delicious food.

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:47.620
Are you just a glutton?

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:51.630
I mean that as much as possible. I just wanna eat good food.

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:54.380
So you are a glutton...

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:57.130
I'm saying that it's important where you eat and whom you eat with.

00:20:01.930 --> 00:20:04.390
<i>He was always saying things like that,</i>

00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:08.940
<i>but in the end, he wasn't able to take in nourishment from his mouth.</i>

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:12.820
<i>God has a cruel streak.</i>

00:20:14.360 --> 00:20:20.160
<i>Seeing Shimao's dishes and utensils being used makes me happy and sad.</i>

00:20:22.030 --> 00:20:24.040
<i>Just like chewing food, swallowing it,</i>

00:20:24.830 --> 00:20:27.540
<i>and feeling it warm up your stomach,</i>

00:20:28.580 --> 00:20:31.580
<i>I received so many things from Shimao</i>

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:34.340
<i>and I can feel them right now.</i>

00:20:36.300 --> 00:20:38.170
It didn't last long,

00:20:38.970 --> 00:20:41.890
but when my husband's condition was relatively stable,

00:20:41.890 --> 00:20:44.100
the two of us often went hiking.

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:48.140
Even though it was just us stomping through the muck,

00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:51.770
he looked incredibly happy then.

00:20:55.230 --> 00:20:57.280
I'm sorry for suddenly bringing that up.

00:20:58.740 --> 00:21:00.320
For some reason,

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:06.740
seeing you sitting there eating with such relish really cheers me up.

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:11.420
So I have a proposal.

00:21:12.710 --> 00:21:15.500
Would you let me wash your back while we take a bath?

00:21:19.970 --> 00:21:25.300
Inside the dreams I always have

00:21:26.430 --> 00:21:31.060
you always smile

00:21:31.060 --> 00:21:35.150
Tell me why

00:21:35.150 --> 00:21:39.030
it won't go away

00:21:39.030 --> 00:21:40.820
I gave you everything

00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:42.660
You gave me everything

00:21:42.660 --> 00:21:47.450
Forever and ever
You're everything,

00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:49.120
still my everything

00:21:49.120 --> 00:21:52.330
I love you

00:21:52.330 --> 00:21:55.710
The songs of midsummer days

00:21:55.710 --> 00:21:58.840
are a fleeting miracle

00:21:58.840 --> 00:22:04.800
like the winter snow

00:22:05.930 --> 00:22:11.810
If I hadn't met you

00:22:11.810 --> 00:22:15.020
I wouldn't have felt this sadness

00:22:15.020 --> 00:22:22.530
and nothing would have pressed down on my dreams

00:22:22.530 --> 00:22:28.200
If I hadn't been able to meet you

00:22:28.200 --> 00:22:35.250
I would never have known the tenderness in strength

00:22:35.250 --> 00:22:40.380
When I close my eyes

00:22:40.380 --> 00:22:44.380
you're right beside me
